<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kharda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Kurdla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kharda was fought in March 1795 near Kharda in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-confederacy">Maratha Confederacy</a> and the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-ali-khan">Nizam Ali Khan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, united for the last time under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a>'s minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanaya">Nana</a> Phadnavis, won decisively, and the Nizam had to cede territory and pay a large indemnity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kharda.jpg" alt="Battle of Kharda" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rushikesh Awatade · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kharda_Fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Defeats by the Marathas at Udgir in 1760 and <b>Kharda</b> in 1795 cost the state large territories.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hyderabad-state">Hyderabad State · Military</a></li></ul></section>
